{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>And a priest's daughter, when she becomes a widow, etc.</b> The verse speaks in the aspect of a soul — of a soul upon which the attachment of evil does not cling at all, but rather she flees and goes on her way as we have said. This is why He gave the reason with בת כהן with a paseq-teshga, to say that this aspect is exceedingly elevated, and therefore no stranger (zar) is with her, as we said concerning her it was stated: ״לֹא יְאֻנֶּה לַצַּדִּיק וְגוֹ׳״ (Proverbs 12:21). And what befalls her is that she becomes a widow and a divorcée. By <b>widow</b> — like a woman who has no husband to sustain and provide for her; so too her husband does not sustain her nor provide for her in mitzvot and good deeds. <b>And divorced</b> — because on account of the fact that the person stretched out his hand to transgress the word of HaShem, he divorced her from himself, as we have written. <b>And she has no seed</b> — that she produced no fruits in this world. Nevertheless, <b>she returns to her father's house</b> — and her return is to eat from her father's table as in the days of her youth, when she would eat in shame from her father's bread she eats — unlike a soul that has attained the performance of Torah and mitzvot, which eats its own labor like a person who eats from what is his own." "And the verse's saying <b>and any stranger (zar) shall not eat holy offerings</b> gives the reason why HaShem blessed be He does not also show mercy to the soul to feed it holy offerings in the manner of grace and lovingkindness. Therefore He stated the reason: ״וְכָל זָר״ etc. And therefore a soul in which has attached the aspect of evil called zar shall not eat — lest that zar which is attached to it eat."], :book :leviticus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T20:00:20.989855964Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}